course: dictionary
lesson: 4236
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Grandfather is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Tama's koro, Māori for grandfather, told him how their ancestors sailed by the stars.» Here grandfather means a person: the father of your mother or your father.
explain: The other meaning is a thing. «A grandfather clock counts the swings of its pendulum.» The word clock tells you this is an object, a tall clock that stands on the floor. Ask yourself: does the sentence fit a person, or a thing?
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. «A grandfather counts the swings of its pendulum» makes no sense, so the clock meaning is right. Words for the same person can also differ: Grandad, Granddad, Grandpa and Pop are all loving names for a grandfather. «diDUS» is a loving word for grandad too.
fact: Grandfather means the father of your mother or your father.
fact: Most people have 2 grandfathers.
fact: A grandfather clock is a tall clock that stands on the floor.
fact: A grandfather clock counts time by the swings of its pendulum.
fact: Words for grandfather include Grandad, Granddad, Grandpa, Pop, and koro (Māori).
exercise: «Tama says his koro told him stories about the sea.» What does koro mean? | A kind of boat | *Grandfather | A bright star | A type of clock
exercise: «A grandfather clock counts the swings of its pendulum.» What is a grandfather clock? | A bell in a church | The father of your mother | *A tall clock that stands on the floor | A man who tells tales
exercise: Which person is a grandfather? | Your brother | Your teacher | *Your mum's dad | Your baby cousin
test: «The grandfather clock in the hall chimed at midnight.» Does grandfather mean a person or a thing here? | A person | A cousin | A pendulum | *A thing: a tall clock
test: How many grandfathers do most people have? | 4 | 1 | 3 | *2
exam: Which sentence uses grandfather as a thing? | *«The grandfather clock in the hall chimed eight times.» | «Her grandfather is visiting on Sunday.» | «Her grandfather told stories by the fire.» | «Grandfather made a cake for everyone.»
